spec: specs/optics.md, stage 3

why: stages 0-2 landed. The last stage is the one the theory chapter
  was filed for: a four-parameter lens IS Atkey's parameterised state
  seen from the other side, and PState is Atkey's state in this
  repository. Making that literal is the point.

what: `State.zoom(lens)` — a program over a PART of the state runs
  over the whole, by interpreting State % A into State % S; and
  `PState.zoom(lens)` — a `Lens[S1, S2, A1, A2]` zooms a typestate
  program, the type-changing optic and the type-changing state being
  one picture. Laws on all three platforms.

predict: State.zoom is a split loop like `handle`; PState.zoom is one
  `shift` and is the whole argument of the stage.
